==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|tottered}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|tatered}}, {{m|en|tatird}}, from {{etyl|non|en}}. Originally, it was derived from the noun, but it was later it reanalysed as a past participle ({{suffix|tatter|ed|lang=en}}), whereafter the verb came into being. Compare {{m|en|tatter}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# rent in [[tatter]]s, [[torn]], hanging in [[rag]]s; [[ragged]]
#* {{quote-text|year=1919|author={{w|Boris Sidis}}|title=[[s:The Source and Aim of Human Progress|The Source and Aim of Human Progress]]|passage=''The chattering, irrational brute of the subconscious clothes itself in the '''tattered''' garments of rationality and idealism.''}}
# [[dress]]ed in [[tatter]]s or [[rag]]s; [[ragged]]
#* {{RQ:Crane Red Badge of Courage|10|101|The '''tattered''' man waved his hand.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[dilapidated]]; showing [[gap]]s or [[break]]s; [[jagged]]; [[broken]]

